## Work planned
`evidence/failure05.18/CONTRACT.md` states the reporting repair before code. The module remains `labs/capture-handoff-pass01/handoff.py`. The public call stays `perform(binding_path)`, with keyword-only `hook`, `pins`, and `fault`. `fault` is a private in-process seam. The CLI stays `perform --binding` and gains no fault switch.

CH-03 separates the capture attempt and the observed member from the adapter's own record writes. A capture the tool reported as captured, followed by a stop or a later error, reports that the member files were observed and remain retained even when `completed.json` is absent. The failure record keeps the reserved inspection as an earlier phase with its time. The current `inspect` field is a later observation, or null when that later read is not safe. Exact tool stdout is kept. `return_inspect` is the status interface. `verify` runs only after that later status is `complete`, because verify refuses a reserved member. A missing success code is not evidence that the child wrote nothing. A listing that does not show `return.md`, `manifest.json`, and `receipt.json` says `capture-files absent`. Pins, timeout, a failed inspection, or bytes that cannot be read say `unknown` or `unverified`. The listing touches only the explicit member, its `payload` directory, the record directory, and the failure-log path.

CH-04 catches `OSError` and a controlled refusal while writing the failure log. Stdout keeps the original handoff reason, adds the secondary log error, and returns exit 2 without a traceback. Partial log bytes stay. An existing log is not overwritten. The error path does not write `completed.json` and does not turn an incomplete capture into success. Programming errors are not caught as a successful result.

A child timeout is recorded before the wait ends. Any captured stdout is kept, and the member outcome stays unknown until a later pin-safe observation. A partial intent write and a partial or readback-failed completed write stay on disk and are not called a completed handoff. Retries do not delete those bytes, do not redraw them, and do not capture again.

The clean success path still launches show, inspect, capture, verify, and inspect, in that order. An identical completed retry still writes nothing, including no new failure log.

## Out of scope
No `app/librarian.py` wiring, no live job, and no model. `perform` does not call queue, claim, return, or reserve. Nothing is deleted, resumed, cleaned, or allocated around a partial. A verified receipt is custody. It is not review, acceptance, acknowledgement, closure, or publication. No second receipt or package validator is added.

## Limits
The same-user gap between a hash read and a later write remains open. A pin or source change found before the completed record stops the record and keeps the conflict. This is not an operating-system sandbox. File-symlink creation may skip on WinError 1314. The bytes-changed-before-capture race is rechecked, not closed. A later observation can itself fail; that failure stays unverified and does not erase the attempt.

