That clean event is `4c2cce50409912edf49d817c5cb061d6514c8a37361a0aebea6b602c302edf3f`. Its disposable receipt is `007c9db193cb03a0bcadc8f1bd3572c344302d68d6a50c6e249104d938e54f7c`. The retry printed `writes none` and left the tree unchanged.

`python -B labs/capture-handoff-pass01/demo.py` exited 0. It printed `result complete`, `not approved`, `not accepted`, and `not published`, then `writes none` on the retry, then `demo failure-log absent`, then the line that this demo is custody only. Demo event `60a65cb50b87216ac377efa9569390fee082cfc7286d7cc06f9fbc4cbdf83bd7`. Demo receipt `1bf833cd7d1f16b5cde0009fa347f3cce2ff398fa485364a2adbc7ac0c22a038`. Those disposable directories were removed.

The repaired stop immediately after capture still begins `attention: stopped after-capture` and ends `result attention`. It also reports `member-written observed`, `custody complete`, `observed-record intent.json`, `record-absent completed.json`, `handoff-complete no`, and the retained `return.md` path. The failure record's current `inspect.status` is `complete`. Its `before-capture` phase stays `reserved`. `tool_stdout` still contains `result captured`. `completed.json` is absent. The retry does not finish the record, does not overwrite the log, and does not change the receipt. The same member report holds for a stop before the final record and for a source change after capture. A pin change after capture reports `custody unverified`, keeps the member files, stores no current inspection, and does not launch verify.

A capture timeout reports `tool timed out: capture`, `capture-child unknown`, and `capture-files absent`, with no `return.md` and no phrase that the child wrote nothing. The retry stops at `intent is retained` and does not capture. A partial intent file stays `partial\n`, with `handoff-complete no`, and the retry does not redraw it or capture. A partial completed file stays `partial\n`; the retry refuses `completed handoff record is not readable` and does not capture. A readback fault leaves the full payload, refuses `record write did not land intact: completed.json` with `handoff-complete no`, and the later call is the existing read-only identical retry.

A failure-log `OSError` before any bytes leaves no file. Stdout still starts with the original pin reason, then `reporting-error failure log: OSError: injected failure-log write error`, and returns exit 2 with no traceback. A partial failure log stays `partial\n` across the retry and is not overwritten.

The earlier Prime stop reported only the intent write, the failure-log write, and `result attention`, while the member already held `return.md`, the manifest, the receipt, and the payloads, and the log still carried the reserved inspection. An injected failure-log `OSError` then escaped uncaught. Those two reports are the before-example in `evidence/prime-review05.17/verification.json`. This repair does not rewrite that file or `0139`.

File symlink creation returned WinError 1314, so that case was skipped. The same-user gap remains open. This module is not an operating-system sandbox. No pinned tool, app file, or live member was edited. Review stays pending. The receipt that follows is custody, not acceptance.
